{"id":"perizzites","name":"Perizzites","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:perizzites"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Perizzites","text":"Villagers; dwellers in the open country, the Canaanitish nation inhabiting the fertile regions south and south-west of Carmel. “They were the graziers, farmers, and peasants of the time.” They were to be driven out of the land by the descendants of Abraham (Gen. 15:20; Ex. 3:8, 17; 23:23; 33:2; 34:11). They are afterwards named among the conquered tribes (Josh. 24:11). Still lingering in the land, however, they were reduced to servitude by Solomon (1 Kings 9:20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6522","lemma":"פְּרִזִּי","xlit":"Pᵉrizzîy","gloss":"a Perizzite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Perizzite","count":7,"share":0.7},{"strong":"H2850","lemma":"חִתִּי","xlit":"Chittîy","gloss":"a Chittite, or descendant of Cheth","kjv":"Hittite, Hittities","count":6,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H3669","lemma":"כְּנַעַנִי","xlit":"Kᵉnaʻanîy","gloss":"a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan","kjv":"Canaanite, merchant, trafficker","count":6,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H2983","lemma":"יְבוּסִי","xlit":"Yᵉbûwçîy","gloss":"a Jebusite or inhabitant of Jebus","kjv":"Jebusite","count":5,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H567","lemma":"אֱמֹרִי","xlit":"ʼĔmôrîy","gloss":"an Emorite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Amorite","count":5,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H2340","lemma":"חִוִּי","xlit":"Chivvîy","gloss":"a Chivvite, one of the aboriginal tribes of Palestine","kjv":"Hivite","count":4,"share":0.4}],"verses":["Gen.13.7","Gen.15.20","Exod.3.8","Exod.23.23","Deut.20.17","Judg.3.5","Ezra.9.1","Judg.3.6","Judg.3.7","Ezra.9.2"],"related":[{"id":"canaanites","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"jebusites","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.127,"why":"7 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"hittites","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.118,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":